474	\section{Parametric Dose-Response Model Comparison}
475	\label{sec:parametric_dr}
476	
477	We fit four parametric dose-response models---Constant (intercept-only), Linear, Quadratic, and four-parameter Hill \citep{hill1910aggregation,ritz2015dose}---to pooled multi-seed MMLU accuracy trajectories for each family. Table~\ref{tab:aicc_dr} reports AICc and Akaike weights.
478	
479	\begin{table}[h]
480	\centering
481	\caption{AICc model selection for dose-response trajectories (pooled multi-seed MMLU). Bold indicates best-fitting model per family; $w$ is the Akaike weight of the best model.}
482	\label{tab:aicc_dr}
483	\footnotesize
484	\begin{tabular}{lccccc}
485	\toprule
486	Family & Constant & Linear & Quadratic & Hill & Best ($w$) \\
487	\midrule
488	Phi-4 14.7B & $-$71.42 & $-$72.08 & $-$70.06 & $\mathbf{-73.14}$ & Hill (0.58) \\
489	Qwen2.5-14B & 49.54 & 23.40 & 21.22 & $\mathbf{18.28}$ & Hill (0.55) \\
490	Qwen2.5-7B & $-$12.38 & $-$20.53 & $-$14.52 & $\mathbf{-24.97}$ & Hill (0.77) \\
491	Gemma-2 9B & $\mathbf{17.35}$ & 18.89 & 20.01 & 18.96 & Constant (0.39) \\
492	OLMo-2 7B & $\mathbf{25.82}$ & 26.66 & 27.54 & 26.47 & Constant (0.62) \\
